{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>The lizard</b> — the name of a creature. And perhaps it is the creature likened to a human in form and appearance, and the proof that it is a creature is 'it grasps with its hands,' meaning it grasps whatever is given to it; it is found in a king's palace on account of its wisdom. These four are wise, and the one who guards [them] is fit to learn from them the way of the world."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:40.888664566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}